## 🧾 Bill of Materials (BOM)

| Qty | Part | Notes |
|-----|------|-------|
| 1 | Seeed Studio XIAO ESP32-C3 | Main controller |
| 1 | 1.9" ST7789 display module (76 x 284, 8-pin header) | Shows the time and games |
| 1 | 1x08 pin socket, 2.54 mm | Display header (J1) |
| 4 | Mechanical keyboard switch, Cherry MX style (Redragon ZT02 model) | SW1-SW4 |
| 1 | Buzzer, 12 mm x 9.5 mm, 7.6 mm pin pitch | BZ1 |
| 4 | M3 screw, about 10-12 mm | Case assembly |
| 1 | Custom PCB (`Production/gerbers.zip`) | 2-layer |
| 1 | 3D printed case: top + bottom (`Production/Top.step`, `Production/Bottom.step`) | |

## 📁 Repository layout

```text
CAD/         GameClock.step   - full assembled clock (PCB + case)
PCB/         KiCad project (.kicad_pro, .kicad_sch, .kicad_pcb) + 3dmodels/
Firmware/    GameClock/GameClock.ino  (Arduino IDE, XIAO ESP32-C3)
Production/  gerbers.zip, Top.step, Bottom.step
```

## 🔧 Firmware

Open `Firmware/GameClock/GameClock.ino` in the Arduino IDE, install **Adafruit GFX Library** and **Adafruit ST7735 and ST7789 Library**, choose the board **XIAO_ESP32C3** and upload.
